  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Jai Prakash Chourasia vs The State Of Jharkhand on 30 January, 2024 Author: Ananda Sen Bench: Ananda Sen In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi W.P.(C) No. 2976 of 2022 ----- Jai Prakash Chourasia, S/o Late Sambhu Nath Chourasia .... Petitioner(s). Versus 1.The State of Jharkhand 2.The Adjudicating Officer-cum-Sub-Divisional Officer, P.O. & P.S. Dhanbad Dhanbad 3.The District Food Safety Officer-cum-Adjudicating Officer-cum-Deputy Commissioner, Dhanbad 4.The food Safety Officer, Dhanbad 5.The Director of Referral Food Laboratory, Government of India ... Respondent(s). ------ Coram : Sri Ananda Sen, J. For the Petitioner(s) : Mr. Rahul Kumar Gupta, Advocate Mr. Rakesh Kr. Singh, Advocate Ms. Swati Singh, Advocate For the Respondent(s) : Mr. Vishal Kr. Rai, Ac to G.A.Iv ......... 05 /30.01.2024:",
    "facts": "2. Petitioner in this writ petition has prayed for the following relief:- I. For issuance of appropriate writ/ direction for setting aside the order dated 12.05.2022 passed by learned adjudicating officer-cum-additional Collector, Dhanbad passed in Food Safety Case No.05/2021, by which the petitioner has been inflicted with a penalty of Rs.3,00.000/- under Section 3(1)(zx) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 [hereinafter the Act] for a product being substandard in terms of the Act. 3. State has filed a counter affidavit taking a preliminary objection that this order, which is impugned in this writ petition, is appeable under Section 17(i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "arguments": "4. Considering the statement made in the counter affidavit, learned counsel for the petitioner seeks permission to withdraw this writ petition to approach the District Food Safety Tribunal by invoking under Section 17(i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006."
  },
